<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Al-Ashraf Musa (Ayyubid sultan of Damascus)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1178–1237</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Al-Ashraf Musa was an Ayyubid prince, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-adil">al-Adil</a>, who ruled the Jazira from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harran">Harran</a> and later became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> in 1229. In 1230 he took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baalbek">Baalbek</a> from its emir Bahramshah. He defeated the Khwarazmian ruler Jalal al-Din with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuks</a> of Rum at Yassıçemen in 1230.</p></div>
